flowchart TB
  accTitle: Website account handover to DorkOS Cloud
  accDescr: Without a valid configured accounts origin the website serves local accounts. When configured, selected browser routes redirect and machine calls proxy to the accounts origin. Managed connections are a separate migration. This diagram describes code behavior, not the production switch state.
  browser["Browser · account pages / navigation"]
  machine["App / machine · account and instance calls"]
  site["Website route-specific forwarding<br/>DORKOS_CLOUD_ACCOUNTS_ORIGIN"]
  local["Website account implementation<br/>Fallback while origin unset or invalid"]
  accounts["Configured Cloud account origin<br/>Separate hosted browser surface"]
  managed["Managed connections<br/>Excluded from account forwarding<br/>Disabled on website when forwarding is on"]
  public["Public website remains<br/>Docs · marketing · marketplace<br/>Separate public migration history"]
  browser --> site
  machine --> site
  site -->|"Unset / invalid origin"| local
  site -->|"Configured: 307 redirect<br/>Account pages + eligible navigation"| accounts
  site -->|"Configured: proxy bearer / body / background calls<br/>Selected account + instance routes; preserve query"| accounts
  site -->|"Separate migration"| managed
  site -->|"Public routes stay local"| public
